---
import { Layers } from '@lucide/astro';
import EmailCta from '../EmailCta.astro';
import { roleEmailCtas, visitorModes } from '../../lib/email-drafts.mts';
---

<section class="mode-hero" aria-labelledby="ops-heading">
  <div class="headline-row">
    <span class="headline-icon" aria-hidden="true"><Layers size={86} /></span>
    <h1 id="ops-heading">
      Website System: from visitor traffic to signed deals and contracts.
    </h1>
  </div>
  <div class="cta-row">
    <EmailCta cta={roleEmailCtas.ops[0]} mode={visitorModes.ops} />
    <EmailCta cta={roleEmailCtas.ops[1]} mode={visitorModes.ops} />
    <EmailCta cta={roleEmailCtas.ops[2]} mode={visitorModes.ops} />
  </div>
  <p class="cta-note">
    This page explains how this website works as a system: traffic sources, page
    roles, visitor flows, CTA actions, and conversion outcomes.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="card" aria-labelledby="ops-goal">
  <h2 id="ops-goal">Website System Goal</h2>
  <p>
    Primary goal: route the right visitors into the right pages and convert
    qualified conversations into signed roles, contracts, and repeat engagements
    without lowering delivery quality.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="card" aria-labelledby="ops-pipeline">
  <h2 id="ops-pipeline">Visitor Flow Stages</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Traffic source: direct, referral, LinkedIn, and peer shares.</li>
    <li>
      Intent routing: visitor selects hiring, build, vision, developer, or this
      system page.
    </li>
    <li>
      Page value: each route gives role-specific proof and a clear next step.
    </li>
    <li>CTA action: visitor sends a low-friction first-contact message.</li>
    <li>Qualification: role/scope fit, timeline, and decision ownership.</li>
    <li>Signed outcome: role offer, paid engagement, or follow-on mandate.</li>
  </ol>
</section>

<details class="card" aria-labelledby="ops-details-summary">
  <summary id="ops-details-summary"
    ><strong>Operational Details</strong></summary
  >

  <section aria-labelledby="ops-cadence">
    <h2 id="ops-cadence">System Operating Cadence</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Daily: triage inbound messages and respond by priority.</li>
      <li>
        Weekly: review visitor volume, CTA clicks, and conversation quality.
      </li>
      <li>
        Bi-weekly: refine role-page copy, CTA prompts, and qualification rules.
      </li>
      <li>
        Monthly: update proof artifacts from shipped work and signed outcomes.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="ops-capacity">
    <h2 id="ops-capacity">Capacity and Scale Constraints</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Current execution mode is solo and quality-gated.</li>
      <li>Pilot delivery capacity remains intentionally limited.</li>
      <li>
        Scale trigger is sustained qualified pipeline, not vanity traffic.
      </li>
      <li>
        Team expansion starts only when pipeline supports predictable,
        repeatable throughput.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="ops-controls">
    <h2 id="ops-controls">Website-to-Deal Quality Controls</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No inflated claims: evidence boundaries are explicitly declared.</li>
      <li>Role clarity: each page states who it is for and what to do next.</li>
      <li>CTA clarity: first contact asks for minimal input only.</li>
      <li>
        Deal discipline: scope and acceptance rules are explicit before start.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="ops-roadmap">
    <h2 id="ops-roadmap">Website System Roadmap</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Increase qualified inbound from hiring and operator channels.</li>
      <li>
        Publish compact case snapshots with measurable, non-sensitive outcomes.
      </li>
      <li>
        Improve per-route conversion from page visit to conversation start.
      </li>
      <li>
        Shift from solo execution to organization mode as signed flow compounds.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</details>
